  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Through FY2026 to date, General Services Administration contract obligations total $19.4B. Obligations are down 18.4% year over year while the agency has made 934,899 awards at an average award size of $20.8K. The FY2026 total is a partial, fiscal year to date number; prior full-year obligations were $23.8B in FY25 and $26.5B in FY24. Computer Systems Design Services and Engineering Services are the largest category recipients so far, with $4.1B and $3.4B respectively. Other sizable categories include Automobile Manufacturing at $2.3B and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $1.2B. On the vendor side, BOOZ ALLEN HAMILTON INC leads with $1.7B in obligations, followed by SCIENCE APPLICATIONS INTERNATIONAL CORPORATION at $870M and several large systems and vehicle suppliers including FORD MOTOR CO at $631M and GENERAL MOTORS LLC at $607M. The data show where current buying is concentrated and which companies are winning the largest shares of FY2026 to date obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How much is GSA spending so far in FY2026?",
        "body": "GSA has $19.4B in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Obligations are down 18.4% year over year. The agency has issued 934,899 awards with an average award size of $20.8K. This FY2026 total is a partial, fiscal year to date figure."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are the biggest goods and services GSA is buying now?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services and Engineering Services are the top categories at $4.1B and $3.4B respectively. Automobile Manufacturing accounts for $2.3B and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounts for $1.2B. Several R&D and professional services categories also appear in the top 10, including a $990M R&D line and $1.1B in All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services."
      }
    ]
  },
